// Bytes and text: a []byte and a string convert both ways, as Go's
// []byte(s) and string(bs).

// Bytes is the bytes of s, a copy: a change to them never reaches s.
func Bytes(s string) []byte { stringsBytes(s) }

// FromBytes is the text of bs. It copies the bytes, as Go's string(bs),
// unless bs is consumed (nothing reads it after the call: a local dead
// after it, or a fresh result), when the text takes the bytes over with no
// copy (types.md, Bindings 2, consumed arguments): a program that builds a
// []byte and then makes it a string pays one buffer, not two.
func FromBytes(bs []byte) string { builderText(bs) }

extern go ergo.local/prototype/runtime/v1.StringsBytes func stringsBytes(s string) []byte
